# A rounded rectangle: opposite straights match, and four 90-degree corners close.
name "Camber Loop"
description "Wide banking, a rising causeway, and changing road widths on a flowing lap."
width 16
start 0 0 0 90

# Width changes blend across the following command. Open the main straight out.
straight 60
width 18
straight 120
checkpoint

# Split the corner into entry, held banking, and exit; climb onto the causeway.
right 20 radius 85 rise 1 bank -14
right 50 radius 85 rise 5 bank -14
right 20 radius 85 bank 0
width 15
bridge 160
checkpoint

# Unwind the bank before each straight and return gently to the lower road.
right 20 radius 85 bank -14
right 50 radius 85 rise -5 bank -14
right 20 radius 85 rise -1 bank 0
width 14
straight 180
checkpoint

# The narrower return side rewards a tidy line through the same-radius bends.
right 20 radius 85 bank -10
right 50 radius 85 bank -10
right 20 radius 85 bank 0
width 16
straight 160
checkpoint
right 20 radius 85 bank -12
right 50 radius 85 bank -12
right 20 radius 85 bank 0

# Exact position, heading, elevation, bank, and starting width meet at the seam.
close
